.TH ORO-LAUNCHER 3 "" "Oro Runtime" "Oro Runtime API Manual"
.SH NAME
oro:launcher \- JavaScript API module
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
import * as module from 'oro:launcher'
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Android named destinations and Linux desktop actions. Requires `[launcher] enabled = true`. A shortcut produces routing receipts, never authorization or resource mutation. Restore sign\-in and resolve the exact current account/target before opening it. iOS/iPadOS, macOS and Windows backends for this publication API are not implemented. `getStatus()` reports unavailable with a reason; operational calls reject ENOSYS. Linux desktop actions do not implement Android pinning.
.SH REFERENCE
.TP
\fBgetStatus()\fR
Reads native launcher support without publishing destinations.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherStatus>\fR
.TP
\fBreplace(destinations)\fR
Replaces this runtime's dynamic destinations, preserving unrelated app shortcuts. Linux publishes a separate owned desktop entry containing actions; it does not overwrite the installed app entry or request pinning. Changed publications invalidate old routing generations, including copied entries. Removed Android targets are disabled, including pinned copies. At most 16 entries and Android's per\-activity quota. Must run from a visible window.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIdestinations\fR (LauncherDestination[]; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherPublicationResult>\fR
.TP
\fBpin(id)\fR
Requests Android's user\-controlled pin flow for an existing destination. Linux rejects ENOSYS. Submission is not confirmation that the user pinned the shortcut.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIid\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherPinResult>\fR
.TP
\fBgetResponses()\fR
Reads pending cold/warm launch identities after restoring authorization. Reads do not consume receipts. Validate current IAM and handle removed accounts/targets; opening a shortcut must not replay a mutation.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<LauncherReceipt[]>\fR
.TP
\fBacknowledgeResponse(receiptId)\fR
Acknowledges a reconciled or rejected routing receipt. Repeat acknowledgements are allowed. Call only after authenticated target resolution has completed.
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIreceiptId\fR (string; required)
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fIPromise<void>\fR
